Parity disposition: the web <DateRangeFilter> is a PURE presentational component (its only "hook" is
useTranslation; it takes startDate/endDate/the change callbacks/onApply/presets/presetIds as props and renders
two <input type="date"> fields, an optional Apply <Button>, and the composed <DatePresetChips> row — no fetch,
no React-Query, no Promise). It therefore has NO loading / error / stale / offline branch. This surface
reproduces the source's REAL branches faithfully — the always-present date field, the optional Apply action
(web `onApply &&`), and the optional preset row (web `presets &&`, itself populated or a labelled empty state,
delegated to the composed DatePresetChips) — exactly as the in-tree siblings DatePresetChips (0151, the
component this surface composes) and ActiveFilterChips (0147) document and do. Inventing fetch chrome would
fabricate states the source does not have (Honesty Covenant #5 cuts both ways). The active-preset highlight is
the port of the web `useMemo(() => matchPresetId(startDate, endDate))`. Charts/maps: none in source → none here.

